//! The `min-block-size` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property defines the
//! minimum horizontal or vertical size of an element's block, depending on its writing mode. It
//! corresponds to either the `min-width` or the `min-height` property, depending on the value of
//! `writing-mode`.
//!
//! Initial: 0. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: block-size of containing block.
//!
//! Grammar: auto | <box-size> | <anchor-size()>
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-sizing-3/#propdef-min-block-size
//!
//! Author guide:
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/min-block-size
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

